  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "The current best is config_005 (RNA-only, scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650. The multimodal counterpart config_030 (same setup + resnet50, concat fusion) scored 0.632, slightly below the RNA-only baseline, suggesting the image signal via concat fusion is adding noise rather than complementary information. Config_031 changes only the fusion strategy from concat to weighted, isolating whether a learned weighting can downweight the weaker image branch and allow the multimodal model to match or exceed the RNA-only ceiling. This is a minimal, controlled comparison that directly tests whether multimodality can be salvaged with resnet50 before spending remaining budget on a different image encoder (ViT). If weighted fusion recovers the gap, it confirms image has marginal value; if not, it justifies pivoting the last 2 experiments to ViT-based multimodal configs."
}

